  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of syncope and presyncope in the setting of known nonrheumatic mitral valve insufficiency and unspecified cardiac arrhythmia (I49.9, I34.0, R55). Due to the intermittent nature of these symptoms and the need to correlate clinical events with underlying rhythm disturbances, long-term continuous ECG monitoring is indicated to evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of collapse. CPT 93247, representing a long-term continuous electrocardiogram monitoring study, is medically necessary to address these documented conditions."
